--TEST--
A property access through a `mixed` receiver is ADR 0036 § 4's name-keyed fetch, with the receiver's own tag checked at the same place — ADR 0007 § 2, § 7 row 13
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `mixed` is ADR 0007 § 2's one unchecked position, so `$m->name` defers
// every question it raises — is this an object, and does that object carry
// this name — to run time, exactly where PHP answers them. It is the fourth
// receiver shape ADR 0036 § 4's erased half covers, and the only one whose
// *tag* nothing proved before the fetch.
final class Box {
    public string $name = "boxed";
    public int $count = 1;

    public function constructor() { }
}

mixed $m = new Box();
echo $m->name, " ", $m->count, "\n";

// The write lands on the value itself: `mixed` erases the static view of a
// refcounted instance and nothing else about it.
$m->name = "wrote";
var $same = $m;
echo $same->name, "\n";

// A name the concrete class does not carry is § 4's catchable throw, the
// same one a plain `object` receiver takes.
try {
    echo $m->nope, "\n";
} catch (Throwable $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}

// A receiver that is not an object at all is the throw this receiver shape
// adds, in PHP's own wording. Every *statically* non-object receiver is
// `E0495` at check time instead — see the companion case.
mixed $five = 5;
try {
    echo $five->name, "\n";
} catch (Throwable $readOnInt) {
    echo $readOnInt->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $five->name = "x";
} catch (Throwable $writeOnInt) {
    echo $writeOnInt->message, "\n";
}

array<string> $rows = ["k" => "v"];
mixed $asArray = $rows;
try {
    echo $asArray->k, "\n";
} catch (Throwable $readOnArray) {
    echo $readOnArray->message, "\n";
}

// `?->` still short-circuits on the `null` tag before any of that, so a
// `mixed` holding `null` answers `null` rather than throwing.
mixed $nothing = null;
echo $nothing?->name ?? "short-circuited", "\n";

// A shape behind a `mixed` binding is reached by name like any other value:
// the fetch never had a slot to rely on in the first place.
mixed $shape = {label: "anonymous"};
echo $shape->label, "\n";

// A freshly built receiver has no other owner, so this is also the row that
// says the base is released and the read is not.
echo (new Box())->name, "\n";
--EXPECT--
boxed 1
wrote
`Box` has no field `nope`
attempt to read property `name` on int
attempt to assign property `name` on int
attempt to read property `k` on array
short-circuited
anonymous
boxed
